Outlook for Linux: give the app its own profile directory.

Upstream derives the config path from app.getPath("userData") before the config
file is loaded, so this has to be set here rather than through config.json.
Keeping it separate stops this app sharing a cache, Local Storage and config.json
with a co-installed Teams for Linux.

app.setPath throws when the target directory does not exist (per the Electron app
docs), and while appData exists this child of it does not, so create it first.
--- a/app/index.js
+++ b/app/index.js
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
   session,
 } = require("electron");
 const path = require("node:path");
+const fs = require("node:fs");
 const crypto = require("node:crypto");
 const CustomBackground = require("./customBackground");
 const CustomStickers = require("./customStickers");
@@ -74,6 +75,12 @@
   process.exit(1);
 });
 
+// Outlook for Linux: a profile of its own, kept out of a co-installed Teams for
+// Linux. setPath throws when the directory is missing, so create it first.
+const outlookProfile = path.join(app.getPath("appData"), "outlook-for-linux");
+fs.mkdirSync(outlookProfile, {recursive: true});
+app.setPath("userData", outlookProfile);
